PATCH 474: the AH-64 weapon-station step 91b8, its five station handlers (88d1/888c/8916/8995/895b) and
the dispense-placement helper 9a50 (board:0007 base-loss sweep, reached once combat runs).

91b8 (asm 0x91b8-0x9205) dispatches `lcall word[CS:0x9206 + station*2]` -- a FAR-pointer table of five
0f69: entries, one per weapon station (the station byte[di+0x91] is pre-scaled by 2).  Ghidra deref'd that
CS table as a host pointer (`(undefined2 *)(byte*2 + -0x6dfa)`) and made the call near, so the first AH-64
that reached a firing state SEGV'd; it also host-deref'd the locked target word[di+0x97] and the callout
table byte[DGROUP:0x91a0+n].  Each station handler is the patch-429 idiom -- `dec rounds; a265 aim;
b1df(type) -> SI=the NEW projectile, DI=the firer; launch wrapper; reload; c047 report` -- with b1df's
CF/SI now correct per patch 462; the cannon (8995) is rate-gated on (word[0x6cde]&7)==0 and the flare
dispenser (895b) reports 0x3031 when empty.  9a50 places a dispensed object at its parent using 03a9's
published DX lane and posts e1d1 for the NEW object (Ghidra wrote that result into the parent).
